            <ArticleTitle>Surgical management of abdominal aortic aneurysm in the high-risk patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>269-79</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical therapy of aortic abdominal aneurysms has progressed in recent years to the point where the presence of an aortic aneurysm greater than 4 cm is an indication for surgical repair. The high-risk patients require careful preoperative evaluation and intensive postoperative supervision if significant morbidity and mortality are to be kept to less than 6 to 7 per cent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
